Package: DCal
Type: Package
Title: Doubly-Calibrated Treatment Effect Estimation
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Xinbo", "Wang", email = "cinbo_w@sjtu.edu.cn", role = c("cre", "aut")),
    person("Liu", "Liu", email = "linliu@sjtu.edu.cn", role = "ctb"),
    person("Yuhao", "Wang", email = "yuhaow.thu@gmail.com", role = "ctb"))
Maintainer: Xinbo Wang <cinbo_w@sjtu.edu.cn>
Description: Implements a novel Double-Calibration (DCal) strategy for estimating treatment effects and other semiparametric parameters in high-dimensional settings. This method corrects the regularization bias from machine learning models (e.g., lasso) used to estimate nuisance functions, requiring only minimal sparsity conditions. Achieves root-n consistency even when one nuisance function is arbitrarily misspecified. Details of the methodology can be found in Lin Liu, Xinbo Wang, and Yuhao Wang (2023) "Root-n consistent semiparametric learning with high-dimensional nuisance functions under minimal sparsity" <arXiv:2305.04174>. The package relies on the optimisation software 'MOSEK' <https://www.mosek.com/> which must be installed separately; see the documentation for 'Rmosek'.
